WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.040
You need to understand that
everything you do at the poker

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.438
table conveys information.

00:00:03.438 --> 00:00:05.190
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.437
You can't be like all loosey-goosey,
having a sandwich,

00:00:07.437 --> 00:00:08.520
being on your phone.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:09.020
Woo-hoo!

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.240
Baby, I love it.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.220
There's three basic
characteristics that

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.660
make an elite poker player.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.760
One is just the raw skill.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.220
The other is a
fundamental understanding

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.630
of the mathematical side.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:25.180
The third part is what
I call discipline.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.630
In this MasterClass, I'm going
to share things that I've

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.470
actually never shared before.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.930
For example, I look at a guy
and say, you've got King Nine.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.040
You're a sick human.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.720
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.540
King Nine!

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:36.600
Well, that's not magic.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.130
It's usually based off
a combination of things.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:40.880
And I'm going to teach
you how to do that.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.940
I'm going to teach you
tournament strategy,

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.340
continuation betting,
picking up tells.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:51.452
So this tell probably
made me the most money.

00:00:51.452 --> 00:00:54.000
The classic chip glance tell.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.330
You notice that?

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.030
I see those cards, and my
brain is telling my eyes,

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:00.070
the next thing we've
got to do is bet chips.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.300
Most of the time, it's
totally subconscious.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.640
They don't even know
they're doing it.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.470
Poker is an
intellectual endeavor

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.600
that is totally skill-based
in the long run.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.520
A lot of people can
confuse themselves

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.980
into thinking that they're
losing because of luck when

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:13.970
it's actually skill.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.560
One of the absolute
best ways to learn

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:21.500
is to go over a hand in
depth in a hand breakdown.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.040
I bet $1,150, and Alec
makes it just $2,500.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.860
I still think his range
can be relatively wide.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.710
Now, on the river, you're pretty
much down to just two options.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:32.960
Is this a value bet,
or is this a bluff?

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.030
There's no such thing
as a value bluff.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:35.630
OK?

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:38.510
You just didn't know
what you were doing.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:40.370
You're going to make
a lot of mistakes.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.909
Learning nothing from those
mistakes is the mistake.

00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:45.075
And when you feel like
you've got this game mastered

00:01:45.075 --> 00:01:46.710
and you've got
nothing left to learn,

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.710
that's the exact point
where everyone else

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.240
starts to surpass you.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:56.040
I'm Daniel Negreanu, and
this is my MasterClass.

